SUMMARY:Tenacious Women: A History of Preservation in New England
LOCATION:Faneuil Library\, 419 Faneuil St\, Brighton\, MA 02135
DESCRIPTION:At the forefront of New England's preservation movement were wo
 men bringing a passion for preservation to the communities where they live
 d. Yet\, somehow\, these tenacious women's history is often overlooked or 
 lost from the record. This lecture will trace women's participation in pre
 servation through the late 19th and early 20th centuries and elevate their
  contributions in preserving New England's history. Our speaker will be El
 izabeth Paliga\, who has been on the staff of Historic New England as the 
 Senior Preservation Services Manager for Northern New England since 2021.\
 nhttps://bpl.bibliocommons.com/events/6aa409f76059b704112a32a8\nFrom Pushp
 in Boston: https://pushpin.city/boston/
